      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author relates two distinct mixed classical/quantum graphical formalisms while respecting copyable classical names and linearly used quantum registers. The construction uses polarized correctness to orient proof-nets as DAGs and normal-form polarized cores to recover networks, then identifies factor semantics up to marginalization. The counted bidirectional representation theorem retains these specialized constructions; ordinary factor positivity and proof-net support are not split into separate items.",
